IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 (Western Australia), with the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive)
-- Regulations 2014 that set its ages, stages, conditions and demerit points -- when I may drive as a learner and on a
-- provisional licence, what my demerit points do to me, what disqualification does to my licence, and when I am driving
-- without authorisation.
--
-- SEAT: the learner and the licensed driver. Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it: "Am I old enough for a
-- learner's permit?", "Who may supervise me?", "May I drive at 1 a.m. on my P plates?", "How many points does my speeding
-- carry?", "When do my points expire?", "How long am I disqualified?". Where the Act or the regulations give a judgment to
-- the CEO (of the Department of Transport) or a court -- a waiver for undue hardship, a permit to drive, a court's
-- disqualification -- that judgment is asked as a fact and the answer is conditional on it.
--
-- Provisions covered. Act: s 2 and s 66 (commencement; permits issued under the Road Traffic Act 1974); s 3 ("driver's
-- licence", "provisional licence"); s 10 and s 11A (the learner's permit); s 16, s 17, s 18 (losing a provisional licence;
-- the unlicensed would-be provisional driver); s 21 and s 23 (effect of disqualification); s 24(1), (3), (4) (when I may
-- apply to remove a long disqualification); Part 4: s 40 (novice drivers; "dealt with by infringement notice"), s 41, s 43,
-- s 44, s 45, s 46, s 48, s 49, s 50, s 51, s 52. Regulations: r 4 (novice driver (type 1A)), r 9 (provisional licence),
-- r 10 (night-time restriction), r 11 (passenger restriction) with r 94, r 15 and r 22(2)-(4) (minimum licence age and its
-- waiver), r 16A (a new applicant under 25 for a car licence), r 35(1) and Sch 7 (conditions that limit authorisation),
-- r 36 (P plates), r 42(3), r 43 (who may supervise), r 44 (minimum age for a learner's permit), r 45, r 46 and Sch 8,
-- r 47, r 48 (learner conditions), r 53 (suspending a permit), r 53A-53C (disqualification: cancel or suspend), r 55, r 57
-- (driving without a licence), r 65 and r 66 (demerit point offences and their points). Road Traffic Code 2000 r 17(1),
-- (2) (the points for speeding, which r 65(3) adopts).
--
-- Edition. Act: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 47952, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47952.txt; no compilation number stated; its compilation table ends with the Road
-- Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Amendment (Driving Restrictions) Act 2024 (No. 45 of 2024, in force 16 November 2024).
-- Regulations: Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Regulations 2014, version 00-ba0-00, currency start 1 July 2026
-- (mrdoc 49701, retrieved 19 October 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../../road-traffic-authorisation-to-drive-regulations-2014/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49701.txt; compilation table
-- to SL 2026/63 (in force 1 July 2026). Road Traffic Code 2000, version 05-aa0-00, currency start 14 May 2026 (mrdoc 49388,
-- retrieved 19 October 2026), as deposited at ../../../road-traffic-code-2000/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49388.txt,
-- used only for r 17 (speeding points), because r 65(3) of the regulations makes the Code's points the demerit points.
-- The regulations are encoded as they stand in that version. Where the compilation table shows that a rule began after a
-- life event (r 11, 1 December 2024), the rule carries its start date; other amendments are not unwound.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Part 2 Division 3A (identity information); s 4, s 5A, s 61 (powers to make regulations); s 8 (the residence
-- and earlier-licence bar on a driver's licence) and s 9 beyond a comment; s 13 to s 15 and r 58 to r 63 (interstate and
-- foreign licences); Part 3 Division 3 (extraordinary licences) beyond s 23's exception; s 53 to s 60 (postponement under
-- s 54 and s 55 is noted, not computed); Parts 5 and 6 other than s 66; the alcohol interlock scheme (s 5A, Part 5A of the
-- regulations); licence classes beyond the car and motor cycle, Sch 4 to Sch 6, r 21; renewal and fees (r 37 to r 39,
-- Part 7); the holiday-period calendar of r 67 (asked as a fact); the offence of driving without authorisation itself
-- (Road Traffic Act 1974 s 49 -- this Act and the regulations say when I am not authorised, the 1974 Act makes it an
-- offence and sets the penalty; not encoded); the dollar value of a penalty unit.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 (WA) and Regulations 2014`

§§ `dates and helpers`

-- s 2: "(b) the rest of the Act, on the day fixed under the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 section 2(b)". Compilation
-- table: "Act other than s. 1 and 2: 27 Apr 2015 (see s. 2(b) and Gazette 17 Apr 2015 p. 1371)". Regulations r 2: they "come
-- into operation on the day fixed under the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 section 2(b)" -- the same day.
`the day the Act and the regulations came into operation` MEANS Date 27 4 2015

-- Regulations compilation table: "Transport Regulations Amendment (Road Traffic) Regulations 2024 Pt. 3 SL 2024/237 ...
-- 1 Dec 2024". r 11: "[Regulation 11 inserted: SL 2024/237 r. 7.]"
`the day the passenger restriction came into operation` MEANS Date 1 12 2024

GIVEN `born on` IS A DATE
      `on`      IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`age in completed years` MEANS
    IF     DATE_MONTH `on` GREATER THAN DATE_MONTH `born on`
        OR (DATE_MONTH `on` EQUALS DATE_MONTH `born on` AND DATE_DAY `on` AT LEAST DATE_DAY `born on`)
    THEN DATE_YEAR `on` MINUS DATE_YEAR `born on`
    ELSE DATE_YEAR `on` MINUS DATE_YEAR `born on` MINUS 1

-- Whole months from one day to a later one ("16 years and 6 months of age" is 198 completed months from birth).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
      `the end`   IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`completed months between` MEANS
        (DATE_YEAR `the end` MINUS DATE_YEAR `the start`) TIMES 12
    PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the end` MINUS DATE_MONTH `the start`)
    MINUS (IF DATE_DAY `the end` LESS THAN DATE_DAY `the start` THEN 1 ELSE 0)

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is on or after` MEANS Day `a` AT LEAST Day `b`

-- "At the end of a period of 3 years after the day on which ..." (s 10(4), s 48). The period starts the day after, so it
-- ends at the end of the third anniversary of the day: still running on the anniversary, over the day after.
-- (A 29 February start is not handled.)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `on`      IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is within 3 years after` MEANS
        `is on or after` `on` `the day`
    AND Day `on` AT MOST Day (Date (DATE_DAY `the day`) (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 3))

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
      `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `2, 66 -- does this Act govern me`

-- s 66: "A learner's permit issued to a person under the RT Act section 43(1) that was in effect immediately before
-- commencement day is, on and from commencement day, to be taken to be a learner's permit issued under section 10(1)."
@export Does the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 govern my permit or licence on this day (s 2)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this Act govern my authorisation to drive on` IF
    `is on or after` `the day` `the day the Act and the regulations came into operation`

@export Is my learner's permit from before 27 April 2015 now taken to be a learner's permit under this Act (s 66)?
GIVEN `issued under the Road Traffic Act 1974 section 43(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your permit was issued under the Road Traffic Act 1974 s 43(1)
      `in effect immediately before 27 April 2015` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was still in effect the day before the Act began
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my old permit taken to be a learner's permit under this Act` IF
    `issued under the Road Traffic Act 1974 section 43(1)` AND `in effect immediately before 27 April 2015`

§§ `10, 11A; r 44-46 -- my learner's permit`

-- s 10(5): the regulations "may fix the minimum age below which, unless the CEO is satisfied that denial of the permit would
-- occasion undue hardship or inconvenience, a person cannot be issued with a learner's permit."
-- r 44(1): "A person who has not reached 16 years of age cannot hold a learner's permit unless -- (a) subregulation (2)
-- applies; or (b) under subregulation (3), the CEO waives the requirement". (2): "A person who has reached 15 years and
-- 6 months of age may hold a learner's permit authorising the person, while learning, to drive only a moped." (3): the CEO
-- may waive "if the CEO is satisfied that denial of the permit would occasion undue hardship".
@export Am I old enough to hold a learner's permit (Regulations r 44)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you would hold the permit
      `for a moped only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the permit is to learn to ride only a moped
      `the CEO waived the age for undue hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO has waived the minimum age because refusing would cause you undue hardship
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I old enough to hold a learner's permit` IF
        `age in completed years` `my date of birth` `the day` AT LEAST 16
    OR  (`for a moped only` AND `completed months between` `my date of birth` `the day` AT LEAST 186)
    OR  `the CEO waived the age for undue hardship`

-- s 10(1): "The CEO may issue to a person a learner's permit". The Act and regulations say when the CEO cannot:
-- r 44 (age); r 45: "Before a person can hold a learner's permit the person must have satisfied the CEO that the person can
-- demonstrate the knowledge of the traffic laws ... referred to in regulation 20" unless waived under r 22(5) (the
-- theory test); r 46 and Sch 8: for some classes, a prerequisite licence held for a time (none for a car, class C, and none
-- for a restricted motor cycle or moped licence, r 46(5)); s 11A(2), (3): evidence of "identity and residential address in
-- this State", and "a photograph taken at the time of the application" and "a signature made at the time" (or one given in
-- the previous 10 years, s 11A(6)). Past those bars the CEO "may" issue: the answer stays conditional on the CEO.
DECLARE `Learner's permit answer` IS ONE OF
    `not yet: I am under the minimum age`
    `not yet: I must first show knowledge of the traffic laws (the theory test)`
    `not yet: I must first hold the prerequisite licence in Schedule 8`
    `not yet: I must first give proof of identity and WA address, and a photograph and signature`
    `yes, if the CEO decides to issue it`

@export Can I be issued a learner's permit (s 10, s 11A; Regulations r 44 to r 46)?
GIVEN `old enough` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you meet the minimum age (see the learner's permit age question)
      `passed the theory test or had it waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have shown the CEO knowledge of the traffic laws and safe driving, or the CEO waived it
      `hold any prerequisite licence Schedule 8 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold the licence Schedule 8 requires for this class (nothing is required for a car or a moped)
      `gave identity, WA address, photograph and signature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given proof of identity and WA address, and a photograph and signature
GIVETH A `Learner's permit answer`
DECIDE `Can I be issued a learner's permit` IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `old enough`) THEN `not yet: I am under the minimum age`
           IF (NOT `passed the theory test or had it waived`) THEN `not yet: I must first show knowledge of the traffic laws (the theory test)`
           IF (NOT `hold any prerequisite licence Schedule 8 requires`) THEN `not yet: I must first hold the prerequisite licence in Schedule 8`
           IF (NOT `gave identity, WA address, photograph and signature`) THEN `not yet: I must first give proof of identity and WA address, and a photograph and signature`
           OTHERWISE `yes, if the CEO decides to issue it`

-- s 10(4): "The permit expires at the end of a period of 3 years after the day on which it is issued unless it has terminated
-- before then, and the CEO may cancel it at any time by notice in writing". r 53: "The CEO may suspend a learner's permit by
-- notice in writing". r 42(3): "The authorisation that a learner's permit gives ... ceases if the holder is granted a
-- driver's licence authorising the kind of driving that the holder was learning".
@export Is my learner's permit in force on this day (s 10(4); Regulations r 42(3), r 53)?
GIVEN `the day it was issued` IS A DATE @desc The day your learner's permit was issued
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about
      `cancelled or suspended by the CEO` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO has cancelled or suspended it by written notice
      `granted a licence for the driving I was learning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since been granted a driver's licence for that kind of driving
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my learner's permit in force` IF
        `is within 3 years after` `the day it was issued` `the day`
    AND (NOT `cancelled or suspended by the CEO`)
    AND (NOT `granted a licence for the driving I was learning`)

§§ `10(2); r 43, 47, 48 -- who may supervise me, and on what conditions`

-- s 10(2): "The permit does not authorise driving except in the course of driving instruction by -- (a) the holder of a
-- licence issued under the Motor Vehicle Drivers Instructors Act 1963; or (b) anyone else prescribed in the regulations."
-- r 43(2): "(a) a person who is an instructor in a youth driver education course conducted or supervised by a body
-- authorised by the CEO ...; or (b) a person who is authorised to perform any driving of a kind for which the driving
-- instruction is to be given and has had that authorisation for a period of, or periods adding up to -- (i) in the case of
-- the driving of a moped, at least 2 years; or (ii) in any other case, at least 4 years." (3): "authorised means authorised
-- by an Australian driver licence or a foreign driving authorisation". A provisional licence counts; a learner's permit does
-- not (it is not an Australian driver licence, s 3).
DECLARE Supervisor IS ONE OF
    `a licensed driving instructor`                  -- s 10(2)(a)
    `a youth driver education course instructor`     -- r 43(2)(a)
    `another licensed driver`                        -- r 43(2)(b), if held long enough
    `nobody qualified`

-- r 47(3): "Whenever the learner drives on a road a motor vehicle to which a learner's permit applies -- (a) the learner must
-- be accompanied by the instructor; and (b) the speed of the motor vehicle must not exceed 100 km/h at any time."
-- r 48(1): the authorisation "does not apply while the vehicle is being driven in contravention of the condition specified in
-- regulation 47(3)(a) but continues to apply while the vehicle is being driven in contravention of any other condition."
-- So driving alone on a permit is driving without authorisation; driving at 110 km/h with the instructor is a breach of
-- condition (r 48(2), 4 PU) but still authorised.
DECLARE `My learning drive` HAS
    `my permit is in force`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am driving solely to learn`               IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10(1), r 42(2)
    `my supervisor`                              IS A Supervisor
    `years my supervisor has held a licence for this kind of driving` IS A NUMBER  -- r 43(2)(b)
    `I am learning to ride a moped`              IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 43(2)(b)(i)
    `my supervisor accompanies me`               IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 47(3)(a)

@export May this person supervise my driving on a learner's permit (s 10(2); Regulations r 43)?
GIVEN `the supervisor` IS A Supervisor @desc Who is supervising you
      `years held` IS A NUMBER @desc For another licensed driver: years they have held a licence for the kind of driving you are learning
      `learning a moped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are learning to ride a moped
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May this person supervise me` IF
    CONSIDER `the supervisor`
    WHEN `a licensed driving instructor` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a youth driver education course instructor` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another licensed driver` THEN
        IF `learning a moped` THEN `years held` AT LEAST 2 ELSE `years held` AT LEAST 4
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Does my learner's permit authorise this drive (s 10; Regulations r 42, r 47, r 48(1))?
GIVEN `the drive` IS A `My learning drive` @desc The drive you are asking about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my learner's permit authorise this drive` IF
        "s 10(4)"     ... `the drive`'s `my permit is in force`
    ... "s 10(1)"     ... `the drive`'s `I am driving solely to learn`
    ... "s 10(2), r 43" ... `May this person supervise me` (`the drive`'s `my supervisor`) (`the drive`'s `years my supervisor has held a licence for this kind of driving`) (`the drive`'s `I am learning to ride a moped`)
    ... "r 47(3)(a), r 48(1)" ... `the drive`'s `my supervisor accompanies me`

@export What is the fastest I may drive on a learner's permit, in km/h (Regulations r 47(3)(b))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the fastest I may drive on my learner's permit` IS 100

-- r 48(2): "The holder of a learner's permit must not contravene the condition specified in regulation 47(3)(b) or any other
-- condition. Penalty for this subregulation: a fine of 4 PU. Modified penalty for this subregulation: 2 PU."
@export What is the most I can be fined for breaking a learner's permit condition, in penalty units (Regulations r 48(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for breaking a learner's condition` IS 4

§§ `r 15, 22, 16A -- when I can hold a driver's licence`

-- r 15(1): "The minimum age that a person must have reached to hold a driver's licence is -- (a) except as stated in
-- paragraph (b), 17 years of age; (b) for a moped licence, 16 years of age." (3): the CEO may waive it under r 22(2).
-- r 22(2): the CEO may waive the age if "(a) denial of a licence would occasion undue hardship; and (b) the requirements of
-- subregulation (3) or (4) that apply are satisfied." (3): if a person with parental responsibility resides in the State,
-- such a person "must have consented in writing"; (4): if none resides in the State, written consent of a person with
-- parental responsibility, or an employer's written confirmation that "the licence is considered essential".
@export Am I old enough to hold a driver's licence (Regulations r 15, r 22(2) to (4))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you would hold the licence
      `a moped licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licence is a moped licence
      `the CEO waived the age for undue hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO has waived the age because refusing would cause undue hardship
      `the written consent or employer confirmation r 22 requires was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a parent (or, if none lives in WA, a parent or employer) gave the written consent or confirmation r 22 requires
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I old enough to hold a driver's licence` IF
        `age in completed years` `my date of birth` `the day` AT LEAST (IF `a moped licence` THEN 16 ELSE 17)
    OR  (`the CEO waived the age for undue hardship` AND `the written consent or employer confirmation r 22 requires was given`)

-- r 16A applies to "a new driver's licence applicant for -- (a) a car licence if the applicant has not reached 25 years of
-- age". (2): "(a) driving the motor vehicle on a road for at least 50 hours, including at least 5 hours of driving the vehicle
-- at night ..., in the course of instruction by" an instructor or a r 43(2) person; "(b) making a record ... signed by the
-- person who gave the instruction; and ... in a logbook approved by the CEO; and (c) having reached 16 years and 6 months of
-- age, a test approved by the CEO and conducted not less than 6 months after the learner's permit was granted ..., satisfying
-- the CEO that the applicant has sufficient ability to recognise hazards on roads; and (d) after completing the requirements
-- set out in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) and having reached 17 years of age, satisfying the CEO that the applicant is able to
-- control the motor vehicle." Passing each test is the CEO's judgment, asked as a fact.
DECLARE `My driving experience` HAS
    `my date of birth`                     IS A DATE
    `the day my learner's permit was granted` IS A DATE
    `supervised hours logged`              IS A NUMBER   -- r 16A(2)(a)
    `of them, night hours`                 IS A NUMBER   -- r 16A(2)(a)
    `logged in an approved logbook, signed by my supervisors` IS A BOOLEAN -- r 16A(2)(b)
    `I passed the hazard perception test`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 16A(2)(c)
    `the day of the hazard perception test` IS A DATE
    `I passed the practical driving assessment` IS A BOOLEAN -- r 16A(2)(d)
    `the day of the practical driving assessment` IS A DATE

@export Have I shown I can drive safely, as a new applicant under 25 for a car licence (Regulations r 16A)?
GIVEN `my experience` IS A `My driving experience` @desc Your logbook hours and test results
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I shown I can drive safely for a car licence` IF
        "r 16A(2)(a)" ... `my experience`'s `supervised hours logged` AT LEAST 50
    ... "r 16A(2)(a)" ... `my experience`'s `of them, night hours` AT LEAST 5
    ... "r 16A(2)(b)" ... `my experience`'s `logged in an approved logbook, signed by my supervisors`
    ... "r 16A(2)(c)" ... `my experience`'s `I passed the hazard perception test`
    ... "r 16A(2)(c): 16 years 6 months" ... `completed months between` (`my experience`'s `my date of birth`) (`my experience`'s `the day of the hazard perception test`) AT LEAST 198
    ... "r 16A(2)(c): 6 months on the permit" ... `completed months between` (`my experience`'s `the day my learner's permit was granted`) (`my experience`'s `the day of the hazard perception test`) AT LEAST 6
    ... "r 16A(2)(d)" ... `my experience`'s `I passed the practical driving assessment`
    ... "r 16A(2)(d): after (c)" ... `is on or after` (`my experience`'s `the day of the practical driving assessment`) (`my experience`'s `the day of the hazard perception test`)
    ... "r 16A(2)(d): 17 years" ... `age in completed years` (`my experience`'s `my date of birth`) (`my experience`'s `the day of the practical driving assessment`) AT LEAST 17

§§ `s 40(2), (3); r 4 -- what kind of novice driver am I`

-- s 40(2): "a person is a novice driver unless the person has, for a period of at least 2 years or periods adding up to at
-- least 2 years, held -- (a) an Australian driver licence; or (b) a licence ... granted ... by an external licensing
-- authority ... other than solely for the purpose of learning". "novice driver (type 2) means a novice driver who has, for a
-- period of at least 1 year ..., held" such a licence; "novice driver (type 1) means a novice driver who is not a novice
-- driver (type 2)". r 4(2): "A person who is a novice driver is a novice driver (type 1A) unless the person has, for a period
-- of at least 6 months or periods adding up to at least 6 months, held a relevant driving authorisation." s 40(3), r 4(3):
-- time "excluded by law from driving" does not count. Time on a learner's permit does not count (s 3).
-- A type 1A novice is also a type 1 novice (type 1A is the first 6 months of type 1).
DECLARE `Novice status` IS ONE OF
    `novice driver (type 1A), and so type 1`
    `novice driver (type 1)`
    `novice driver (type 2)`
    `not a novice driver`

@export What kind of novice driver am I (s 40(2), (3); Regulations r 4)?
GIVEN `months held` IS A NUMBER @desc Months you have held a driver's licence (not a learner's permit), not counting months you were excluded by law from driving
GIVETH A `Novice status`
DECIDE `What kind of novice driver am I` IS
    BRANCH IF `months held` AT LEAST 24 THEN `not a novice driver`
           IF `months held` AT LEAST 12 THEN `novice driver (type 2)`
           IF `months held` AT LEAST 6 THEN `novice driver (type 1)`
           OTHERWISE `novice driver (type 1A), and so type 1`

GIVEN `status` IS A `Novice status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is type 1A` MEANS
    CONSIDER `status`
    WHEN `novice driver (type 1A), and so type 1` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `status` IS A `Novice status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a novice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `status`
    WHEN `not a novice driver` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `r 9, r 36 -- my provisional licence`

-- r 9(2): "The driver's licence granted to a person must be a provisional licence if the person -- (a) is a novice driver;
-- or (b) has not reached 19 years of age." (3): the endorsement "ceases to have effect when the holder of the licence --
-- (a) has ceased to be a novice driver; and (b) has reached 19 years of age."
@export Must my licence be (or stay) provisional (Regulations r 9)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about
      `months held` IS A NUMBER @desc Months you have held a driver's licence, not counting months excluded by law from driving
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my licence be provisional` IF
        `is a novice` (`What kind of novice driver am I` `months held`)
    OR  `age in completed years` `my date of birth` `the day` LESS THAN 19

-- r 36(1): the holder of a provisional licence "must display on the vehicle 2 plates" front and rear (3 PU). (3): "Each plate
-- must bear the letter "P" -- (a) if the driver is a novice driver (type 1A), in white on a red background; or (b) in any
-- other case, in white on a green background." (6): no one else may drive with P plates displayed.
DECLARE `P plates` IS ONE OF
    `red P plates (a white P on red)`
    `green P plates (a white P on green)`
    `no P plates`

@export What P plates must I display (Regulations r 36)?
GIVEN `provisional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your licence is a provisional licence
      `months held` IS A NUMBER @desc Months you have held a driver's licence, not counting months excluded by law from driving
GIVETH A `P plates`
DECIDE `What P plates must I display` IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `provisional`) THEN `no P plates`
           IF `is type 1A` (`What kind of novice driver am I` `months held`) THEN `red P plates (a white P on red)`
           OTHERWISE `green P plates (a white P on green)`

§§ `r 10, r 57(3) -- driving between midnight and 5 a.m.`

-- r 10(2): a licence held by a novice driver (type 1A) "does not authorise the person to drive a motor vehicle on a road
-- during the period between midnight and the following 5 a.m. unless -- (a) the driving is -- (i) in the course of
-- employment; or (ii) for the purpose of travelling to or from employment and by the shortest practicable route ...; or
-- (iii) for the purpose of travelling to or from schooling and by the shortest practicable route ...; and (b) in the case of
-- travel from employment or schooling, the travel commences as soon as is practicable after the employment or schooling
-- ceases." "employment includes both paid and unpaid employment; schooling means a course of education or training for which
-- the person is enrolled." (3): not when "driving in the course of instruction as authorised by regulation 56(1) or (2)".
-- r 57(3): the CEO may give a written permit to a type 1A driver found driving in those hours.
DECLARE `Night purpose` IS ONE OF
    `working (paid or unpaid)`
    `going to work, school or training by the shortest practicable route`
    `coming home from work, school or training by the shortest route, leaving as soon as practicable`
    `coming home from work, school or training, but not leaving as soon as practicable`
    `driving under instruction as r 56 allows`
    `anything else`

@export May I drive between midnight and 5 a.m. (Regulations r 10, r 57)?
GIVEN `months held` IS A NUMBER @desc Months you have held a driver's licence, not counting months excluded by law from driving
      `the purpose` IS A `Night purpose` @desc Why you are driving
      `the CEO gave me a written permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO has given you a written permit to drive (r 57)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I drive between midnight and 5 am` IF
        (NOT `is type 1A` (`What kind of novice driver am I` `months held`))
    OR  `the CEO gave me a written permit`
    OR  CONSIDER `the purpose`
        WHEN `coming home from work, school or training, but not leaving as soon as practicable` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `anything else` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `r 11, r 94 -- how many passengers I may carry`

-- r 11(3): a licence held by a novice driver (type 1A) "does not authorise the person to drive a motor vehicle carrying more
-- than 1 passenger (the permitted passenger) on a road unless -- (a) at least 1 of the passengers is an experienced driver;
-- or (b) each additional passenger is a member of the person's immediate family; or (c) the person -- (i) is required to
-- carry each additional passenger for the person's employment; and (ii) is carrying a document stating that fact signed by
-- the person's employer; and (iii) if requested by a police officer, produces the document". (2): a co-driver is a
-- passenger. (4): an experienced driver is authorised to drive the novice's class and has held that authorisation for "at
-- least 4 years" under a licence "other than a provisional licence". r 94: r 11 applies whenever the licence was granted.
-- r 11 began on 1 December 2024 (compilation table); before then there was no passenger limit in these regulations.
DECLARE `My passengers` HAS
    `number of passengers, counting any co-driver` IS A NUMBER
    `years the most experienced passenger has held a non-provisional licence for my class` IS A NUMBER  -- r 11(4)
    `every passenger after the first is immediate family`   IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 11(3)(b), (1)
    `my employer requires me to carry them, and I carry the employer's signed document` IS A BOOLEAN -- r 11(3)(c)

@export May I carry these passengers (Regulations r 11, r 94)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day of the drive
      `months held` IS A NUMBER @desc Months you have held a driver's licence, not counting months excluded by law from driving
      `the passengers` IS A `My passengers` @desc Who is in the car with you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I carry these passengers` IF
        (NOT `is on or after` `the day` `the day the passenger restriction came into operation`)
    OR  (NOT `is type 1A` (`What kind of novice driver am I` `months held`))
    OR  `the passengers`'s `number of passengers, counting any co-driver` AT MOST 1
    OR  `the passengers`'s `years the most experienced passenger has held a non-provisional licence for my class` AT LEAST 4
    OR  `the passengers`'s `every passenger after the first is immediate family`
    OR  `the passengers`'s `my employer requires me to carry them, and I carry the employer's signed document`

§§ `r 35(1), Sch 7, r 55, r 57; s 23 -- am I authorised to drive at all`

-- r 35(1): "The authorisation that a driver's licence gives to drive a motor vehicle does not apply while the vehicle is being
-- driven in contravention of a condition of the licence described in Schedule 7 column 2" (automatic transmission A, B;
-- learner approved motor cycle E; alcohol interlock I; moped only N; corrective lenses S; under 0.02 BAC Z) "but continues to
-- apply while the vehicle is being driven in contravention of any other condition."
-- r 55: some vehicles need no licence (a power assisted pedal cycle, a slow motorised wheelchair, an electric rideable
-- device, and others). r 57(1): the CEO may in exceptional circumstances permit driving in writing.
-- s 23: "A driver's licence, other than an extraordinary licence, or a learner's permit obtained by a person who is
-- disqualified from holding or obtaining a driver's licence is of no effect." s 17(2), s 21(2): a suspended licence "is of
-- no effect". Driving when not authorised is an offence under the Road Traffic Act 1974 s 49, which is not encoded here.
DECLARE `My drive` HAS
    `my licence or permit covers this class of vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN   -- r 8, r 42, Sch 2
    `it is current, not suspended or cancelled, and not obtained while disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 17(2), s 21(2), s 23, r 37(7)
    `I am disqualified from holding or obtaining a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am breaking a Schedule 7 condition (A, B, E, I, N, S or Z)` IS A BOOLEAN -- r 35(1)
    `I am breaking a novice night-time or passenger restriction` IS A BOOLEAN -- r 10, r 11
    `on a learner's permit, my supervisor is with me or I hold no permit` IS A BOOLEAN -- r 48(1)
    `the vehicle needs no licence under r 55` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the CEO gave me a written permit for this driving` IS A BOOLEAN    -- r 57

@export Am I authorised to drive this vehicle on this drive (Regulations r 35(1), r 48(1), r 55, r 57; s 23)?
GIVEN `the drive` IS A `My drive` @desc Your licence and the drive you are asking about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I authorised to drive` IF
        `the drive`'s `the vehicle needs no licence under r 55`
    OR  `the drive`'s `the CEO gave me a written permit for this driving`
    OR  (    `the drive`'s `my licence or permit covers this class of vehicle`
         AND `the drive`'s `it is current, not suspended or cancelled, and not obtained while disqualified`
         AND (NOT `the drive`'s `I am disqualified from holding or obtaining a licence`)
         AND (NOT `the drive`'s `I am breaking a Schedule 7 condition (A, B, E, I, N, S or Z)`)
         AND (NOT `the drive`'s `I am breaking a novice night-time or passenger restriction`)
         AND `the drive`'s `on a learner's permit, my supervisor is with me or I hold no permit`)

@export Does a licence or permit I obtain while disqualified have any effect (s 23)?
GIVEN `disqualified when I obtained it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were disqualified from holding or obtaining a licence when it was obtained
      `an extraordinary licence ordered by a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is an extraordinary licence granted on a court's order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a licence I obtain while disqualified have effect` IF
    (NOT `disqualified when I obtained it`) OR `an extraordinary licence ordered by a court`

§§ `s 16, 17, 18; r 53A-53C -- what disqualification does to my licence`

-- s 16(1): if the holder of a provisional licence "(a) is convicted of an offence" listed (Criminal Code s 277 arising from
-- driving, s 378 of a motor vehicle; Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 s 32(4), s 36, s 44; Road Traffic Act 1974 s 54,
-- 55, 56, 61, 62, 62A, 64AA, 64AC or 90, or prescribed) "or (b) is disqualified by a court ... (other than the Fines,
-- Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994)" the provisional licence is "by operation of this subsection,
-- cancelled". (3): if "disqualified under Part 4", it is cancelled. s 17(1): a fines enforcement licence suspension order, or
-- a Road Traffic Act 1974 s 71C notice, "suspended so long as the disqualification continues in force".
-- r 53A(2): in Part 3A "a reference to a driver's licence -- (a) does not include a provisional licence". r 53B: a licence or
-- learner's permit is cancelled when a court disqualifies on conviction of an alcohol interlock offence, or of a repeat
-- prescribed offence (RTA s 63, 64, 64AB, 64B(3), 67, 67AA, 67AD(4) or (6); for s 64, a prior within 5 years). r 53C: any
-- other court disqualification, disqualification "by operation of the Act", or a fines licence suspension order --
-- "suspended so long as the disqualification continues in force".
DECLARE `How I am disqualified` IS ONE OF
    `convicted of an offence listed in s 16(1)`
    `disqualified by a court on conviction`
    `disqualified under Part 4 (demerit points)`
    `disqualified by a fines enforcement licence suspension order or a Road Traffic Act s 71C notice`

DECLARE `What happens to my licence` IS ONE OF
    `cancelled`
    `suspended while the disqualification lasts`
    `nothing under these provisions`

@export What happens to my licence or learner's permit when I am disqualified (s 16, s 17; Regulations r 53B, r 53C)?
GIVEN `provisional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a provisional licence
      `how` IS A `How I am disqualified` @desc How you came to be disqualified, or convicted
      `an alcohol interlock offence or a repeat prescribed offence under r 53B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a court disqualification of a full licence or permit: whether the offence is an alcohol interlock offence or a repeat prescribed drink- or drug-driving offence
GIVETH A `What happens to my licence`
DECIDE `What happens to my licence when I am disqualified` IS
    IF `provisional`
    THEN CONSIDER `how`
         WHEN `disqualified by a fines enforcement licence suspension order or a Road Traffic Act s 71C notice` THEN `suspended while the disqualification lasts`
         OTHERWISE `cancelled`
    ELSE CONSIDER `how`
         -- a conviction listed in s 16(1) does not by itself touch a full licence; the court's disqualification, if any, does
         WHEN `convicted of an offence listed in s 16(1)` THEN `nothing under these provisions`
         WHEN `disqualified by a court on conviction` THEN
             IF `an alcohol interlock offence or a repeat prescribed offence under r 53B` THEN `cancelled` ELSE `suspended while the disqualification lasts`
         OTHERWISE `suspended while the disqualification lasts`

-- s 16(2): disqualified "for whichever of the following periods that terminates later -- (a) the period for which the person
-- is disqualified by the court; (b) a period of 3 months from the date of the person's conviction". s 18(3) the same.
-- Reading: both periods are taken to run from the conviction, so the later-ending one is the longer one.
@export For how many months am I disqualified after my provisional licence is cancelled on conviction (s 16(2), s 18(3))?
GIVEN `months disqualified by the court` IS A NUMBER @desc Months the court disqualified you for (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months am I disqualified after losing my provisional licence` IS
    `the greater of` `months disqualified by the court` 3

-- s 18(1): "unlicensed person means a person -- (a) who does not hold a driver's licence; and (b) in respect of whom the
-- regulations would require that if a driver's licence were to be granted to the person, the licence would be a provisional
-- licence." (2): such a person "is disqualified from holding or obtaining a driver's licence if the person is -- (a)
-- convicted of an offence mentioned in section 16(1); or (b) convicted of an offence under the Road Traffic Act 1974 section
-- 49(1)(a) [driving without authorisation]; or (c) disqualified by a court".
DECLARE `What I was convicted of` IS ONE OF
    `an offence listed in s 16(1)`
    `driving without authorisation (Road Traffic Act 1974 s 49(1)(a))`
    `an offence for which a court disqualified me`
    `nothing of that kind`

@export Am I disqualified, as someone without a licence who would get a provisional one (s 18)?
GIVEN `I hold a driver's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a driver's licence (a learner's permit is not one)
      `my licence would have to be provisional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a licence granted to you would have to be provisional (a novice, or under 19)
      `the conviction` IS A `What I was convicted of` @desc What you were convicted of
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I disqualified as an unlicensed would-be provisional driver` IF
        (NOT `I hold a driver's licence`)
    AND `my licence would have to be provisional`
    AND CONSIDER `the conviction`
        WHEN `nothing of that kind` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 24(1): a person disqualified by a court "for a period exceeding 3 years" may apply to a court to remove it. (3): not
-- before "(a) if the disqualification is for not more than 6 years: 3 years; (b) if ... more than 6 years but not more than
-- 20 years: one-half of the period ...; (c) if ... more than 20 years: 10 years." (4): permanent counts as more than 20 years.
@export How many months must pass before I may apply to remove my court disqualification (s 24)? (0 means I cannot apply)
GIVEN `months of disqualification` IS A NUMBER @desc The length of the court's disqualification, in months
      `permanent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are disqualified permanently
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months before I may apply to remove my disqualification` IS
    BRANCH IF `permanent` THEN 120
           IF `months of disqualification` AT MOST 36 THEN 0
           IF `months of disqualification` AT MOST 72 THEN 36
           IF `months of disqualification` AT MOST 240 THEN `months of disqualification` DIVIDED BY 2
           OTHERWISE 120

§§ `s 41; r 65, 66; Road Traffic Code 2000 r 17 -- how many demerit points`

-- s 41(1): "The regulations may prescribe an offence under a road law as a demerit point offence in WA, and specify the number
-- of demerit points". (2): it must involve "the driving or use of a motor vehicle". r 65(3): an offence under the Road Traffic
-- Code 2000 "for which a penalty is expressed as a number of points" is a demerit point offence, "and the number of demerit
-- points applying to the offence is that number of points". r 65(4): not when riding a motorised scooter or electric rideable
-- device.
-- Road Traffic Code 2000 r 17(1), "Exceeding a speed limit by --": (a) "not more than 9 km/h": no points, 2 PU; (b) "more
-- than 9 km/h but not more than 19 km/h": 4 points in a holiday period, otherwise 2; 4 PU; (c) "more than 19 km/h but not
-- more than 29 km/h": 6 / 3; 8 PU; (d) "more than 29 km/h but not more than 40 km/h": 12 / 6; 16 PU; (e) "more than
-- 40 km/h": 14 / 7; 24 PU. r 17(2), a heavy vehicle: the same points; 4, 6, 10, 24 and 30 PU.
-- Whether the day falls in a holiday period (r 67: long weekends, Easter, 17 days from the last Friday before Christmas) is
-- asked as a fact.
@export How many demerit points does my speeding carry (Road Traffic Code 2000 r 17; Regulations r 65(3))?
GIVEN `km/h over the limit` IS A NUMBER @desc How many km/h over the speed limit you were
      `in a holiday period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence was in a holiday period (long weekend, Easter, Christmas)
      `on a motorised scooter or electric rideable device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were riding a motorised scooter or an electric rideable device
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many demerit points does my speeding carry` IS
    BRANCH IF `on a motorised scooter or electric rideable device` THEN 0
           IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 9 THEN 0
           IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 19 THEN (IF `in a holiday period` THEN 4 ELSE 2)
           IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 29 THEN (IF `in a holiday period` THEN 6 ELSE 3)
           IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 40 THEN (IF `in a holiday period` THEN 12 ELSE 6)
           OTHERWISE (IF `in a holiday period` THEN 14 ELSE 7)

@export What is the modified penalty for my speeding, in penalty units (Road Traffic Code 2000 r 17)?
GIVEN `km/h over the limit` IS A NUMBER @desc How many km/h over the speed limit you were
      `driving a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving a heavy vehicle
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the modified penalty for my speeding` IS
    BRANCH IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 9 THEN (IF `driving a heavy vehicle` THEN 4 ELSE 2)
           IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 19 THEN (IF `driving a heavy vehicle` THEN 6 ELSE 4)
           IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 29 THEN (IF `driving a heavy vehicle` THEN 10 ELSE 8)
           IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 40 THEN (IF `driving a heavy vehicle` THEN 24 ELSE 16)
           OTHERWISE (IF `driving a heavy vehicle` THEN 30 ELSE 24)

-- r 65(2) Table (Road Traffic Act 1974 offences), the rows a learner or ordinary driver meets; r 66 (Road Traffic (Vehicles)
-- Act 2012 s 75(1)): 3 points. Rows for alcohol bands, drugs and refusing a sample are left out.
DECLARE `Road Traffic Act offence` IS ONE OF
    `a first offence of driving without authorisation by a type 1A novice, between midnight and 5 a.m. or over the passenger limit (s 49(1))`
    `a first offence of dangerous driving (s 61)`
    `careless driving (s 62)`
    `causing excessive noise or smoke (s 62A)`
    `driving with any blood alcohol, where none is allowed (s 64AAA)`
    `driving with a radar detector fitted (s 81G(2))`
    `the Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act 2012 s 75(1) offence (r 66)`

@export How many demerit points does this Road Traffic Act offence carry (Regulations r 65(2), r 66)?
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Road Traffic Act offence` @desc The offence
      `in a holiday period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was in a holiday period
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many demerit points does this offence carry` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `a first offence of driving without authorisation by a type 1A novice, between midnight and 5 a.m. or over the passenger limit (s 49(1))` THEN 2
    WHEN `a first offence of dangerous driving (s 61)` THEN 6
    WHEN `careless driving (s 62)` THEN 3
    WHEN `causing excessive noise or smoke (s 62A)` THEN 3
    WHEN `driving with any blood alcohol, where none is allowed (s 64AAA)` THEN 3
    WHEN `driving with a radar detector fitted (s 81G(2))` THEN IF `in a holiday period` THEN 14 ELSE 7
    WHEN `the Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act 2012 s 75(1) offence (r 66)` THEN 3

§§ `s 40(1A), 43-46 -- when points are recorded against me`

-- s 40(1A)(b): if the Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 Part 3 applies, an offence is "dealt with
-- by infringement notice" "the first time 1 of the following events occurs -- (i) an amount is paid under the infringement
-- notice (regardless of whether it is the full amount ...); (ii) an order to pay or elect is issued"; (c) "otherwise -- when an
-- amount is paid". (1B): even "a dishonoured payment" counts. (Paragraph (a), notices of another jurisdiction, not encoded.)
@export Has my infringement notice been "dealt with", so that points follow (s 40(1A), (1B))?
GIVEN `the Fines Enforcement Act Part 3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 Part 3 applies to the notice (it does to a WA traffic infringement)
      `I paid something, even if the payment was dishonoured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any amount has been paid, even part, even if dishonoured
      `an order to pay or elect has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an order to pay or elect has been issued to you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I dealt with by infringement notice` IF
        `I paid something, even if the payment was dishonoured`
    OR  (`the Fines Enforcement Act Part 3 applies` AND `an order to pay or elect has been issued`)

-- s 43(1): a WA licence or learner's permit makes WA the registry jurisdiction; (2): another jurisdiction's authorisation
-- makes that jurisdiction it; (3): if neither now, the one previously held, or the most recent; (4): "If this section does
-- not otherwise identify one, and only one, jurisdiction ..., this State is" the registry jurisdiction.
-- A person holding both a WA and an interstate authorisation is identified twice, so (4) makes WA the registry.
@export Is WA my demerit point registry jurisdiction (s 43)?
GIVEN `I hold a WA licence or learner's permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a WA driver's licence or learner's permit
      `I hold another jurisdiction's authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold an interstate licence or permit
      `I held one before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you hold neither: whether you held one before
      `the most recent was from WA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether the most recent was a WA one
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is WA my demerit point registry jurisdiction` IF
        `I hold a WA licence or learner's permit`
    OR  (    (NOT `I hold another jurisdiction's authorisation`)
         AND ((NOT `I held one before`) OR `the most recent was from WA`))

-- s 44(1), s 45(1): demerit point action "is to be taken" against a person for whom WA is the registry jurisdiction, after a
-- conviction or after being dealt with by infringement notice, for a demerit point offence under a road law "or the law of
-- another jurisdiction"; s 44(2), s 45(2): against others only for an offence "under a road law". s 44(3): not if "because of
-- the conviction, the person was disqualified"; (4): disqualification for not paying the fine does not count. s 46: "only
-- against an individual". s 47(2): the CEO records the offence and points in the register.
DECLARE `How my offence ended` IS ONE OF
    `dealt with by infringement notice`
    `convicted, not disqualified because of the conviction`
    `convicted and disqualified because of the conviction`
    `convicted, disqualified only for not paying the fine`
    `not yet dealt with`

@export Will demerit points be recorded against me (s 44 to s 47)?
GIVEN `I am an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an individual (not a company)
      `a demerit point offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence carries demerit points
      `an offence under a WA road law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is an offence under WA law (not interstate)
      `WA is my registry jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WA is your demerit point registry jurisdiction
      `the outcome` IS A `How my offence ended` @desc How the offence has been dealt with
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will demerit points be recorded against me` IF
        `I am an individual`
    AND `a demerit point offence`
    AND (`WA is my registry jurisdiction` OR `an offence under a WA road law`)
    AND CONSIDER `the outcome`
        WHEN `convicted and disqualified because of the conviction` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `not yet dealt with` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 48 -- when my points expire`

-- s 48: "At the end of the period of 3 years after the day on which an offence was committed or allegedly committed, any
-- demerit points applying to the offence expire." s 40: "current demerit points means demerit points that have been recorded
-- in the demerit points register and have not expired or been cancelled". The clock runs from the offence, not the payment.
@export Are the demerit points for this offence still current on this day (s 48)?
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence was committed
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about
      `cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the points have been cancelled (for example by a notice under s 49 or s 50)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are these demerit points current` IF
        `is within 3 years after` `the day of the offence` `the day`
    AND (NOT `cancelled`)

§§ `s 49, 50 -- when I lose my licence for points`

-- s 49(1): "If the number of current demerit points ... reaches at least 12, the CEO is to give the person ... an excessive
-- demerit points notice". (2): "(a) for less than 16 points, 3 months; (b) for at least 16 but less than 20 points, 4 months;
-- (c) for at least 20 points, 5 months, and the day on which the period is stated to commence is to be the 28th day after the
-- notice is given or a later day." (3): the points are cancelled "whether or not the person makes a section 51 election".
-- (4): disqualified if no s 51 election is made. 0 here means no notice is due.
@export For how many months will an excessive demerit points notice disqualify me (s 49)? (0 means no notice is due)
GIVEN `my current demerit points` IS A NUMBER @desc Your current (unexpired, uncancelled) demerit points
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months does an excessive demerit points notice disqualify me` IS
    BRANCH IF `my current demerit points` LESS THAN 12 THEN 0
           IF `my current demerit points` LESS THAN 16 THEN 3
           IF `my current demerit points` LESS THAN 20 THEN 4
           OTHERWISE 5

-- s 50(2): "If the number of postcommencement demerit points ... reaches at least 4 in respect of any offence committed when
-- the person was a novice driver (type 1), or ... reaches at least 8 in respect of any offence committed when the person was a
-- novice driver (type 2), the CEO is to give the person, whether or not the person is still a novice driver, ... an excessive
-- demerit points (novice driver) notice"; (c) "the period of disqualification is 3 months"; (d) it commences "on the day after
-- the notice is given or a later day". (4): disqualified for 3 months; there is no s 51 election. (7): s 49 may also apply.
-- s 50(1) and note 1: postcommencement points exclude offences before 1 December 2010 (the Road Traffic Amendment Act (No. 2)
-- 2007 s 27); every offence here is later.
-- Reading: the count is of all current postcommencement points, and the threshold is fixed by the novice type at the time of
-- the offence that takes the count there.
@export Must I be given an excessive demerit points (novice driver) notice, with 3 months' disqualification (s 50)?
GIVEN `my current points after the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Your current demerit points, counting this offence
      `months held when I offended` IS A NUMBER @desc Months you had held a licence (not counting excluded time) on the day of the offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be given a novice driver notice` IF
    CONSIDER `What kind of novice driver am I` `months held when I offended`
    WHEN `novice driver (type 1A), and so type 1` THEN `my current points after the offence` AT LEAST 4
    WHEN `novice driver (type 1)` THEN `my current points after the offence` AT LEAST 4
    WHEN `novice driver (type 2)` THEN `my current points after the offence` AT LEAST 8
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 49(2): the disqualification starts on "the 28th day after the notice is given or a later day"; s 50(2)(d): "the day after
-- the notice is given or a later day". Both may be postponed under s 54 (an existing disqualification or an election period
-- running), which is not computed here.
@export What is the earliest day my demerit points disqualification can start (s 49(2), s 50(2)(d))?
GIVEN `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the CEO gave you the notice
      `a novice driver notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a novice driver notice (s 50) rather than an excessive demerit points notice (s 49)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `The earliest day my demerit disqualification can start` IS
    IF `a novice driver notice`
    THEN Date (Day `the day the notice was given` PLUS 1)
    ELSE Date (Day `the day the notice was given` PLUS 28)

§§ `s 51, 52 -- the good behaviour election`

-- s 51(1): a person given an excessive demerit points notice "may ... avoid being disqualified ... by making an election ...
-- for the year". (2): "a person must hold a driver's licence other than a provisional licence and must not be a novice
-- driver". (4): in writing "within 21 days after the day on which the CEO gave the excessive demerit points notice".
@export May I avoid the disqualification by electing a good behaviour year (s 51)?
GIVEN `I hold a driver's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a driver's licence
      `it is provisional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a provisional licence
      `months held` IS A NUMBER @desc Months you have held a licence, not counting excluded time
      `days since the notice was given` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the CEO gave you the excessive demerit points notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make a section 51 election` IF
        `I hold a driver's licence`
    AND (NOT `it is provisional`)
    AND (NOT `is a novice` (`What kind of novice driver am I` `months held`))
    AND `days since the notice was given` AT MOST 21

-- s 51(3): I elect not to commit in the year "(a) an offence for which 2 or more demerit points can be recorded ...; or (b)
-- offences for which a total of 2 or more demerit points can be recorded ...; or (c)" one carrying mandatory disqualification
-- by a court, "or (d)" one for which the Act disqualifies on conviction. s 52(1), (4): then a notice disqualifies me for
-- "double the period of disqualification that was stated in the excessive demerit points notice".
@export Have I broken my good behaviour election (s 51(3), s 52(1))?
GIVEN `points recorded for offences in the election year` IS A NUMBER @desc Demerit points recorded for offences committed during the election year
      `convicted of an offence with mandatory or automatic disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were convicted of an offence in that year for which disqualification is mandatory or automatic
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I broken my election` IF
        `points recorded for offences in the election year` AT LEAST 2
    OR  `convicted of an offence with mandatory or automatic disqualification`

@export For how many months am I disqualified after breaking my election (s 52(4))?
GIVEN `months in the excessive demerit points notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The period stated in the original notice, in months
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months am I disqualified after breaking my election` IS
    `months in the excessive demerit points notice` TIMES 2
